{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":2,"timestamp":1791184797,"nonce":"AzVyqE6qD0t+vw6PiRSCsZ3WVXg=","title":"A Slack member cannot link themselves to an oto user, so no one can approve a Remedy from Slack","was":"**What is wrong.** A Remedy can be approved or declined from Slack (ac9b492, 9be848b), but only by a Slack member linked to an oto user who holds the approval grant. Nothing can create that link. `Service.LinkSlackIdentity` (`internal/identity/service/reads.go:329`) has no caller: there is no route, no CLI command and no UI. The unlinked reply tells a member to \"ask whoever runs oto to link\", and nobody can."}]}